# Bumm AI Frontend v3 — Cursor Rules
# Synced with CLAUDE.md. Cursor reads this automatically.

## Project Context
- Bumm AI frontend: Next.js 15 thin client for Solana smart contract platform
- React 19, TypeScript strict, Tailwind CSS 4
- Spec: docs/TECHNICAL_SPEC_V3_1.md, docs/V3_THIN_CLIENT.md

## STRICT Rules
- Functional components ONLY (no class components)
- No `any` types — use proper TypeScript interfaces
- No god components (max 150 lines per component)
- Custom hooks for business logic (useXxx pattern)
- All API calls through service layer, never from components
- Absolute imports via @/ alias
- localStorage keys prefixed with `bumm_`
- No direct backend URLs — use proxy `/api/backend/*`

## Architecture
- src/app/ → App Router pages + API route handlers
- src/components/ → reusable UI (PascalCase files)
- src/hooks/ → custom hooks (useBummApi, etc.)
- src/services/ → API client, business logic
- src/config/ → constants, endpoint definitions
- src/lib/ → utilities
- src/types/ → TypeScript types

## Data Flow (always follow this)
Component → useBummApi hook → bummService → ApiClient → Next.js proxy → Backend

## Styling
- Tailwind CSS 4 utility classes first
- Framer Motion for animations
- GSAP for complex scroll/timeline animations
- Dark theme by default (match existing design)
- Responsive: mobile-first approach

## When Implementing
1. Check existing components for patterns
2. Use useBummApi hook for any backend interaction
3. Handle loading/error states in every component
4. Support mock API fallback gracefully
5. Follow existing naming conventions in src/config/api.ts

## Key Files
- src/hooks/useBummApi.ts — main data hook
- src/services/bummService.ts — API business logic
- src/config/api.ts — endpoint definitions
- src/app/api/backend/[...path]/route.ts — proxy
